#: contribute3.mw:1
msgid ""
"You don’t need to be an expert programmer to help in the development of our "
"platform. You can find different tasks at every skill level. With the help "
"of our developers, you will be able to improve your skills while helping "
"us.\n"
"Contact them at '''[https://chat.wikitolearn.org/channel/tech #tech]''' on "
"the WikiToLearn chat."
msgstr ""
"Nun precises ser un programador espertu p'ayudar nel desendolcu de la nuesa "
"plataforma. Pues alcontrar xeres diferentes en cada nivel d'habilidá. Per "
"duana de los nuesos desendolcadores vas ser a ameyorar eses habilidaes al "
"empar que nos ayudes.\n"
"Contauta con ellos en '''[https://chat.wikitolearn.org/channel/tech "
"#tech]''' na charra de WikiToLearn."

#: contribute3.mw:4
msgid ""
"We also advise you to read the '''[http://meta.wikitolearn.org/"
"Guide_for_the_development_of_WikiToLearn WikiToLearn guide for "
"development]'''."
msgstr ""
"Tamién t'aconseyamos que lleas la '''[http://meta.wikitolearn.org/"
"Guide_for_the_development_of_WikiToLearn guía de WikiToLearn pal "
"desendolcu]'''."

#: contribute3.mw:4
msgid "Code"
msgstr "Códigu"

#: contribute3.mw:7
msgid ""
"All of our code is open-source and you can find it on the '''[https://github."
"com/WikiToLearn WikiToLearn GitHub]'''."
msgstr ""
"Tol nuesu códigu ye abiertu y pues alcontralu nel '''[https://github.com/"
"WikiToLearn GitHub de WikiToLearn]'''"

#: contribute3.mw:7
msgid "Git"
msgstr "Git"

#: contribute3.mw:10
msgid ""
"Git is a software tool used to manage large projects collaboratively. "
"WikiToLearn uses Git to manage the updates and all the changes of the "
"project."
msgstr ""
"Git ye una ferramienta de software usada pa xestionar proyeutos grandes de "
"mou collaborativu. WikiToLearn usa git pa xestionar los anovamientos y tolos "
"cambeos del proyeutu."

#: contribute3.mw:12
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First of all, you will have to '''[https://git-scm.com/ install Git]'''. If "
"you are not familiar on how to use it, you could start with this '''[https://"
"try.github.io/levels/1/challenges/1 15 minutes tutorial]'''. A full git "
"tutorial is provided by '''[https://www.atlassian.com/git/ Atlassian]''', or "
"you can also try the '''[https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-git "
"codeacademy guide]''' (extremely simple)."
msgstr ""
"Lo primero de too, vas precisar '''[https://git-scm.com/ instalar Git]'''. "
"Si nun sabes cómo usalu, podríes apenzar por ver esti '''[https://try.github."
"io/levels/1/challenges/1 tutorial de 15 minutos]'''. '''[https://www."
"atlassian.com/git/ Atlassian]''' forne un tutorial completu de git, tamién "
"pues probar la guía de '''[https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-git "
"codeacademy guide]''' (percenciella)"

#: contribute3.mw:14
msgid ""
"We also suggest you this '''[http://ktown.kde.org/~zrusin/git/git-cheat-"
"sheet.svg cheat sheet]''' with the most used commands."
msgstr ""
"Tamién te suxerimos esta '''[http://ktown.kde.org/~zrusin/git/git-cheat-"
"sheet.svg chuleta]''' colos comandos más usaos."

#: contribute3.mw:14
msgid "Docker"
msgstr "Docker"

#: contribute3.mw:17
msgid ""
"Docker is a software used by WikiToLearn to divide the project into "
"different modules. To run WikiToLearn you will need to '''[https://docs."
"docker.com/engine/getstarted/ install and get started with Docker]'''."
msgstr ""
"Docker ye'l software qu'usa WikiToLearn pa dixebrar el proyeutu en módulos "
"diferentes. Pa executar WikiToLearn vas precisar '''[https://docs.docker.com/"
"engine/getstarted/ instalar y entamar Docker]'''."

#: contribute3.mw:17
msgid "Programming languages"
msgstr "Llinguaxes de programación"

#: contribute3.mw:20
msgid ""
"Due to the complexity of our project, WikiToLearn employs many different web "
"technologies and development environments, but most of it is written in: "
"Python, PHP, CSS, HTML and JavaScript."
msgstr ""
"Pola mor de la complexidá del nuesu proyeutu, WikiToLearn emplega munches "
"teunoloxíes web y entornos de desendolcu diferentes, pero la mayoría d'ellos "
"tan escritos en Python, PHP, CSS, HTML y JavaScript."
